: fixture: anthropic/error-mid-stream
: capture: synthetic
: provider: anthropic
: model: claude-sonnet-4-5
: captured: 2026-08-10
: request: {"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","stream":true,"max_tokens":1024,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"Check that for me."}]}
: source: https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/streaming, "Error events". The error frame below is the documented example copied verbatim: event: error / data: {"type": "error", "error": {"type": "overloaded_error", "message": "Overloaded"}}, described there as what arrives "during periods of high usage ... which would normally correspond to an HTTP 529 in a non-streaming context".
: note: SYNTHETIC because an overloaded_error cannot be requested. The equivalent hunt on the OpenAI side is recorded in openai/in-band-error: every attempt to force a mid-stream failure returned a non-200 instead, which is a different code path. The point of this fixture is that the text streamed BEFORE the error survives on the turn.

